<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of preliminary round,</p>
<p>first leg matches in African club soccer competitions:</p>
<p>Played on Saturday:</p>
<p>Champions' League</p>
<p>In Victoria: St Michel United (Seychelles) 1 FC BFV</p>
<p>(Madagascar) 2 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Saint Michel United - Rakotomanga 50</p>
<p>FC BFV - Tally 13, Mamikely 72</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>In Dar es Salaam: Young Africans (Tanzania) 0 Express</p>
<p>(Uganda) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Played Sunday:</p>
<p>CAF Cup</p>
<p>In Arusha, Tanzania:</p>
<p>Simba (Tanzania)  4  Dire Dawa Locomotive (Ethiopia)  1</p>
<p>(2-1)</p>
<p>Attendance:  10,000</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>Sigara (Tanzania)  1  Dynamos (Zimbabwe)  0  (1-0)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Addis Ababa:</p>
<p>Awassa Flour Mill (Ethiopia)  0  Umeme SC (Uganda)  2  (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Eric Anyole 55, Patrick Mbazira 82.</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>Champions Cup</p>
<p>In Cotonou:</p>
<p>Mogas (Benin)  1  CD Travadores (Cape Verde Islands)  0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer:  Emmanuel Olu Kayode 25.</p>
<p>Attendance: 11,000  </p>
<p>Champions Cup</p>
<p>In Monrovia:</p>
<p>    Junior Professionals (Liberia)  2   Racing Club Bobo</p>
<p>Dialassou (Burkina Faso) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Francis Carr  33,  Kay North 65.</p>
<p>Attendance: 22,000</p>
</text>
